# Ops / Recovery Router

Canon: `AGENTS.md` § Task routing (Ops / recovery). Detail: `docs/agent-workflows/ops-recovery-routine.md`.

## Task class

Route here when work is **operational**, not product implementation:

- dirty root / stash / worktree cleanup
- `/clean-root`, `/plan-run recover`, plan-run state restore
- open PR babysit, CI red triage, branch hygiene
- Linear stale claim / handoff recovery

**Not** implementation or regression — do not touch product code unless recovery contract names paths.

## Dirty worktree

| Mode | Dirty inventory | Edits |
|------|-----------------|-------|
| Implementation / docs / regression | BLOCKED unless user scoped paths | production paths forbidden |
| Ops / recovery | allowed for diagnosis | whitelist only (below) |

## Edit whitelist (recovery only)

- `var/plan-run/**`, `plans/**` — plan-run metadata restore only
- `.worktrees/**` — list/remove stale worktrees when user or skill requests
- governance/skills/docs — when task is explicitly recovery or safety fix
- stash apply/pop, branch switch, worktree add/remove — git state only

Forbidden without explicit user request: product `django_apps/**`, `src/**`, `tests/**`.

## Protected paths — never auto-delete

```text
var/plan-run/**
.worktrees/**
plans/**
documents/**
docs/**
.devtool/**
```

Also never `git clean` target: `.env`, `.env.*` local secrets.

## Ignored cleanup

- **Never** auto-run any `git clean` variant (`-fd`, `-fdX`, `-fxd`, …). See `workflow-safety.mdc`.
- Preview only: `/clean-root clear-ignored` with protected excludes (`clean-root` skill).
- `/clean-root auto` must not delete ignored workflow state.

## Pipeline

```text
inventory → classify risk → safe recovery action → verify state → STOP
```

No commit/push/PR unless user asks. No opening PRs from dirty-root auto chains.

Skills: `/clean-root`, `/plan-run recover`, `babysit` (PR/CI). Do not stack with `/bug-fix` or implementation skills on same turn.
